# Project Rules

## Project Shape
- This project is configured for SwarmForge with four AI-backed agents: specifier, coder, refactorer, and architect. Their CLI backends are configured in `swarmforge/swarmforge.conf`.
- Project languages: {{LANGUAGES}}.
- Before changing code, inspect the repository to identify its build, test, formatting, and dependency commands. Use tools already available in the project or on the local machine.

## Local-Only Tooling
- SwarmForge's own tooling (gherkin parser, gherkin mutator, gherkin IR DRY checker, swarm scripts, swarm-init, prompts) is self-contained. Do not clone, download, install, or update those from a remote repository or package registry.
- Third-party language analysis tools and project dependencies (pytest, coverage, radon, pylint, mutmut, jscpd, npm/pip packages, etc.) may be installed when a task requires them and the user grants permission. Before installing, state the exact install command and ask the user. Do not auto-install.
- Prefer installing into the project's local environment (project venv, pyproject.toml, package.json) when one exists. Ask which tool manager to use if it is unclear.
- If the user declines, stop and report the missing tool instead of skipping the check silently.

## Local Configuration
- Preserve project-local SwarmForge configuration under `swarmforge/`.
- Keep swarm state local under `.swarmforge/`, worktrees under `.worktrees/`, and shared scripts under `swarmforge/scripts/`.

## Handoffs
- Prefer terse, explicit handoffs that report state and request role-appropriate review. Do not include verifications or sender process narrative.

## Ownership
- Do not change another role's prompt or workflow ownership without explicit user direction.
